<Application x:Class="EchoEnvironment.App"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:local="clr-namespace:EchoEnvironment">
    <!--
      StartupUri was REMOVED at Phase 6c (MIGRATION_PLAN 6c). The plan warns that a composition root in
      OnStartup conflicts with StartupUri and that one of the two must go; removing StartupUri is the
      correct choice, because StartupUri constructs the window with a parameterless constructor, which is
      exactly the thing 6c removes - MainWindow now needs to be told which sensor source to use.

      Leaving StartupUri in place would have produced TWO windows: the one WPF opens from the URI, and the
      one App.OnStartup shows. That is not a subtle bug and it is not detectable from a build, which is why
      the plan called this out as "a change to App.xaml, which is XAML and easy to get wrong".

      The window is now constructed in exactly one place: EchoEnvironment/App.xaml.cs, OnStartup.
    -->
    <Application.Resources>

    </Application.Resources>
</Application>
